{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfmeetas","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2009 Paper 1 Offline","year":2009,"examDate":2009,"subject":"physics","chapter":"geometrical-optics","chapterGroup":"optics","topic":"refraction-tir-and-prism","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pa-ball-is-dropped-from-a-height-of-20-m-above-the-surface-jee-advanced-physics-motion-up0f0pqnsb7lzpiy","content":"<p>A ball is dropped from a height of 20 m above the surface of water in a lake. The refractive index of water is 4/3. A fish inside the lake, in the line of fall of the ball, is looking at the ball. At an instant, when the ball is 12.8 m above the water surface, the fish sees the speed of ball as (Take g = 10 m/s<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.887ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 436.6 833.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>)</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"9 m/s"},{"identifier":"B","content":"12 m/s"},{"identifier":"C","content":"16 m/s"},{"identifier":"D","content":"21.33 m/s"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>The velocity of the ball when it has fallen through 7.2 m is</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.639ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"19.213ex\" height=\"2.851ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -977.5 8492.1 1260\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g d